1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.111
Your model is right.

2
00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:05.231
And your users still won't bet on it.

3
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:07.322
That half-second of doubt?

4
00:00:07.323 --> 00:00:09.899
It's the only thing I design.

5
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.251
It ends with the part where I got it wrong.

6
00:00:14.168 --> 00:00:16.679
Everything starts with listening.

7
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.871
And listening means being ready to hear that the brief itself is wrong.

8
00:00:21.872 --> 00:00:27.614
At PTC, the brief said: redesign the UX of five learning platforms.

9
00:00:27.615 --> 00:00:30.125
The research said something else.

10
00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:34.630
Customers didn't recognise any of our five product names.

11
00:00:34.631 --> 00:00:38.323
They already called all of it PTC University.

12
00:00:38.324 --> 00:00:41.071
So the listening overturned the brief.

13
00:00:41.072 --> 00:00:47.659
We retired four of five products and consolidated under the one name customers already used.

14
00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:52.758
Structure is where listening becomes the decision that matters.

15
00:00:52.759 --> 00:01:00.155
At Talon Outdoor — the UK's largest out-of-home agency — the recommendation model was beating the traders.

16
00:01:00.156 --> 00:01:02.690
And they overrode it anyway.

17
00:01:02.691 --> 00:01:07.451
A bare ranked list gives an expert nothing to do with their doubt.

18
00:01:07.452 --> 00:01:09.780
So the model didn't change.

19
00:01:09.781 --> 00:01:12.019
What it handed over did.

20
00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:19.315
A ranked list of billboards became a full campaign plan — KP Is attached, customisable in one click.

21
00:01:19.316 --> 00:01:22.917
Watch the plan reshape when I switch the priority.

22
00:01:22.918 --> 00:01:24.815
ROI first.

23
00:01:24.816 --> 00:01:28.678
Same engine output — a completely different argument.

24
00:01:28.679 --> 00:01:32.076
One a trader can stake their name on.

25
00:01:33.032 --> 00:01:37.128
Proving means the failure modes ship before the feature does.

26
00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:42.495
On the private-equity screener, analysts are paid to doubt confident numbers.

27
00:01:42.496 --> 00:01:45.144
So no score travels alone.

28
00:01:45.145 --> 00:01:47.758
This drawer is the proof surface.

29
00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:49.685
Explain this score.

30
00:01:49.686 --> 00:01:58.125
And the number opens into its sources — the board pack, the audited statements, and the one claim that couldn't be verified.

31
00:01:58.126 --> 00:02:02.288
An honest “I'm not sure” instead of a fluent guess.

32
00:02:03.272 --> 00:02:05.989
Now the part that didn't work.

33
00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:11.112
On PTC's accessibility pass, I did what felt thorough.

34
00:02:11.113 --> 00:02:15.131
Every element loaded with ARIA labels.

35
00:02:15.132 --> 00:02:21.737
Then I tested with real visually-impaired users, and watched it fail in front of me.

36
00:02:21.738 --> 00:02:25.523
They skim — by heading and landmark, fast.

37
00:02:25.524 --> 00:02:31.185
My thorough labels were slowing down exactly the people I built them for.

38
00:02:31.186 --> 00:02:38.342
So I switched my monitor off for a week and navigated the whole system by screen reader alone.

39
00:02:38.343 --> 00:02:44.127
The second version worked because the first one had failed where I could see it.

40
00:02:45.172 --> 00:02:48.271
Landing is measured, with baselines.

41
00:02:48.272 --> 00:02:51.519
Campaign planning: two weeks to three hours.

42
00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.302
Deal screening: sixty percent faster, measured before and after rollout.

43
00:02:57.303 --> 00:03:01.659
A million dollars a year off PTC's print budget.

44
00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:07.816
And subscriptions from zero to sixty-four percent of new bookings — in five quarters.

45
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:13.471
Every one of these is on my homepage with its measurement basis one click deep.

46
00:03:14.384 --> 00:03:15.604
Listen.

47
00:03:15.605 --> 00:03:17.009
Structure.

48
00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.152
Prove.

49
00:03:18.153 --> 00:03:19.437
Land.

50
00:03:19.438 --> 00:03:21.116
That's the job.

51
00:03:21.117 --> 00:03:25.163
I'm looking for one seat where this is the whole job.

52
00:03:25.164 --> 00:03:27.116
Not a phase of it.
